@startuml target_storage_boundaries
title Storage, source identity and trust boundaries
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

package "Trusted workflow code" {
  [Pinned target resolver] as Resolver
  [L0 restore / validation helpers] as Guard
  [Existing L1 transport actions] as Transport
}
package "Ephemeral CPU producer job" {
  [Pinned source checkout] as Source
  [Target container\nnormal CANN OR published nightly runtime] as Runtime
  [Native build + existing hash retention] as Build
  [Verified L0 artifacts] as Artifacts
}
cloud "GitHub Actions Cache\nL0 final artifacts" as GHA
cloud "OBS\nL1 incremental snapshots" as OBS
cloud "Container registry\nruntime and nightly images" as OCI
package "Consumer jobs" {
  [Image source context] as Image
  [PR nightly source checkout] as Nightly
}
package "Existing independent path" {
  [Multi-node Pod / PVC local cache] as Multi
}

Resolver --> Source : pinned SHA / fixed rebase / csrc hash
Resolver --> Runtime : actual FROM or nightly image + SOC + arch
OCI --> Runtime : pull existing published image
Source --> Build
Runtime --> Build
Transport --> OBS : L1 restore; optional trusted save
Transport --> Build : workspace-relative csrc/build_cache
Build --> Artifacts : successful build only
Artifacts --> GHA : actions/cache/save
GHA --> Image : matching regular/image L0 via actions/cache/restore
GHA --> Guard : nightly actions/cache/restore
Guard --> Nightly : validated nightly ABI-specific L0
OCI --> Nightly : runtime image only
OCI --> Multi

note bottom of GHA
  L0 uses native GitHub Cache actions explicitly.
  OBS environment variables cannot redirect these operations.
  GitHub repository/ref visibility and cache eviction remain unchanged.
end note
note bottom of Build
  Workflow helpers are checked out separately from PR source.
  OBS writer credentials are not exported into compilation steps.
  PR consumers receive no L1 writer credentials.
end note
note bottom of OCI
  Existing Dockerfiles, buildx publication and multi-arch merge remain intact.
  This PR does not introduce Docker cp/create/wait/rm orchestration.
end note
@enduml
